  "review": "Correct selector biconditional and AND/OR polarity. Sorted operands preserve all commutative gates. First NOT is evaluated on bank input 0..10; fixed cofactors cover its dependencies. Positive minimal and negative maximal points determine monotone suffix in every cofactor. Final-OR AND-bank mode omits only edge01, and decoder restores that edge with one final gate. Decoder verifies every one of 1024 original inputs and uses correct 11-input wire numbering. This establishes encoder soundness for the restricted templates, not exhaustiveness over arbitrary circuits."
